        "body": "Though they may look similar, てよかった and ばよかった express opposite feelings. てよかった conveys relief or happiness about something that happened, e.g. 行ってよかった ('I'm glad I went.' or literally 'It was good that I went.'). In contrast, ばよかった expresses regret about something that didn't happen, e.g., 行けばよかった ('I wish I had gone.' or literally, 'It would have been nice if I went.').",
